            <div>
              <p>Box breathing, also known as square breathing or 4-4-4-4 breathing, is a structured breathing technique where you inhale, hold, exhale, and hold empty for equal counts. This balanced four-part rhythm is valued for promoting calm and focus. Each of the four phases lasts the same duration, typically 4 seconds, creating a predictable rhythm that makes it one of the most accessible and effective breathwork techniques.</p>
            </div>
