            <div>
              <p>Box breathing is a gentle practice that is generally safe for most people when done correctly. It is often used for staying calm and composed under pressure. However, individuals with epilepsy, high blood pressure, heart conditions, or who are pregnant should consult a doctor before practicing. Always practice in a safe environment — never while driving, in water, or operating machinery. Stop immediately if you experience chest pain or severe dizziness.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </details>

